class Solution {
    public int[][] merge(int[][] intervals) {
        List<int[]> intervalList = new ArrayList<>();
        Arrays.sort(intervals, (a,b) -> a[0]-b[0]);
        int start = intervals[0][0], end = intervals[0][1];
        for(int i=1; i < intervals.length; i++){
            int nextStart =  intervals[i][0];
            int nextEnd =  intervals[i][1];
            if(nextStart <= end){
                end = Math.max(end, nextEnd);
            }
            else{
                intervalList.add(new int[]{start, end});
                start = nextStart;
                end = nextEnd;
            }
            
        }
        intervalList.add(new int[]{start, end});
        return intervalList.toArray(new int[0][]);
    }
}

Time : O(n log n) + O(n)
Space : O(n) {Additional stace for result list and sorting takes O(n) space in worst case -> creates temp array and recursion stack space)
